79.	 Substance Use Disorders
Abuse of substances such as marijuana, benzodiazepines, heroine, 
cocaine etc. is prevalent in many communities around the country. 
Typically, individuals with such disorders request help only after they 
are forced to do so by family members. They may also begin to have 
withdrawal symptoms when on admission for serious physical illness. 
This is because they have no access to the substance being abused. This 
may complicate treatment of the primary disease for which they were 
admitted. 
Causes 
yy
Social factors
yy
Peer pressure (e.g. family members, friends)
yy
Lack of coping skills (e.g. with life’s difficulties, aids to coping in 
times of trouble)
yy
Addiction
yy
Tolerance (increased requirement of substance to maintain the same 
feeling) 
yy
Withdrawal effects (unpleasant effects lead to a return to drug use)
Symptoms 
Cannabis withdrawal
yy
Insomnia 
yy
Shakiness 
yy
Irritability 
yy
Restlessness 
yy
Anxiety 
yy
Anger
yy
Onset: Within 24 hours of drug use
yy
Duration: 1-2 weeks
