Physical appearance 
yy
Sweating, tremor, agitation, problem with coordination, gait. Rate these ap­
pearances and reassess them at regular intervals to monitor the progress 
of symptoms. If symptoms are increasing in severity, notify a senior staff 
member, or if available, a doctor
Suicide risk assessment 
yy
To determine the level of risk at a given time and to provide appropriate 
clinical care and management. Possible suicidal behaviour includes thinking 
about suicide, harming oneself or attempting suicide. 
yy
Screening questions of suicide risk: 
yy
Have things been so bad lately that you have thought you would rather 
not be here?
yy
Have you had any thoughts of harming yourself?
yy
Are you thinking of suicide?
yy
Do you have any plans to commit suicide?
yy
Have you ever tried to harm yourself?
yy
Have you made any current plans?
yy
Do you have access to any thing with which to hurt yourself? 
