yy
Care of children (assess possible neglect or physical or sexual abuse of chil­
dren or exposure to such harm from others and intervene to protect as 
soon as possible or refer to appropriate agency)
yy
Drug use of cohabitants
yy
Current legal issues
yy
Financial problems
yy
Work commitments
Treatment 
Treatment objectives
yy
To provide supportive care (information, stress reduction, 
reassurance)
yy
To teach coping skills (relaxation techniques, dietary guidelines, 
methods to reduce craving for the substance, sleep disturbance 
management)
yy
To manage difficult behavior (anxiety, agitation, panic and aggression)'),
