87.	 Pityriasis Versicolor
Pityriasis versicolor is a common yeast infection of the skin, in which 
flaky discoloured patches appear on the chest and back. It is sometimes 
called tinea versicolor. It is more common in hot climates, and often affects 
people that perspire heavily. It is a disorder of the healthy but florid cases 
are seen in the immunosuppressed such as those with diabetes mellitus, 
HIV/AIDS and topical steroid abuse.
