Viral Skin Infections 
88.	 Herpes Simplex Infections 
These are acute self-limiting viral infections of the skin and mucous 
membranes resulting in blistering eruptions usually seen on the face 
(called “cold sores”) or the genitalia.  Recurrence is common on previously 
affected skin areas and is due to proliferation of virus within the epidermis 
of the affected dermatome. Extensive lesions may be associated with an 
immunocompromised state or atopy.
