95.	 Acne Vulgaris 
Acne vulgaris (pimples or spots) is a common chronic inflammatory 
skin disorder involving the hair follicle and sebaceous gland which 
presents mainly in adolescence. A variety of spots appear mostly on the 
face and other parts of the body. Severe acne may require evaluation 
