Treatment 
Treatment objectives
yy
To relieve symptoms
yy
To prevent acute hyperglycaemic complications (i.e. ketoacidosis and 
the hyperosmolar state)
yy
To prevent treatment-related hypoglycaemia
yy
To achieve and maintain appropriate glycaemic targets
yy
Fasting blood glucose between 4-7 mmol/L (less intensive gly­
caemic targets in elderly patients)
yy
2-hour post-meal blood glucose between 5-9 mmol/L (less in­
tensive glycaemic targets in elderly patients)
yy
Glycated haemoglobin 7 % or less (less intensive glycaemic tar­
gets in elderly patients)
yy
To ensure weight reduction in overweight and obese individuals
yy
To prevent chronic complications of diabetes by maintaining
yy
The glycaemic targets noted above
yy
Blood pressure less than 130/80 mmHg
yy
LDL-cholesterol less than 2.5 mmol/L

