105.	Hyperthyroidism 
Excess thyroid hormone in the blood results in hyperthyroidism 
(thyrotoxicosis). If left untreated, significant weight loss, eye and cardiac 
complications, may occur. Addition of extra iodine to the diet (e.g. as in 
iodated salt) is not the recommended treatment and may, in fact, worsen 
the condition. 
